<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{DOMAIN}}{{PREFIX}} · getBible API</title>
{{HEAD_ICONS}}<style>{{CSS}}</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<header class="brand">
{{#IF LOGO_URL}}<a href="/"><img src="{{LOGO_URL}}" alt="getBible"></a>
{{/IF}}<div>
<h1>{{DOMAIN}}{{#UNLESS IS_ROOT}} <code>{{PREFIX}}</code>{{/UNLESS}}</h1>
<p class="lead">{{#IF IS_ROOT}}The getBible static API at <code>{{DOMAIN}}</code>: every resource is a file served exactly as published.{{/IF}}{{#UNLESS IS_ROOT}}Version <code>{{LABEL}}</code> of the getBible static API at <code>{{DOMAIN}}</code>: every resource below this prefix is a file served exactly as published.{{/UNLESS}} <span class="badge">{{ACCESS_MODE_LABEL}}</span></p>
</div>
</header>

<h2>Base URL</h2>
<pre><code>https://{{DOMAIN}}{{PREFIX}}</code></pre>
<p>Documents are addressed by their path below the base URL:</p>
<pre><code>curl https://{{DOMAIN}}{{PREFIX}}{{EXAMPLE_PATH}}</code></pre>
{{#IF OPENAPI_URL}}<p>The machine-readable description of this endpoint is <a href="{{OPENAPI_URL}}">openapi.json</a>.</p>
{{/IF}}
<h2>How to call it</h2>
<ul>
<li>Allowed file types: {{EXTENSIONS_LIST}}. Nothing else exists here.</li>
<li>Methods: <code>GET</code>, <code>HEAD</code>, <code>OPTIONS</code>. Anything else answers <code>405</code>. Query strings answer <code>400</code>.</li>
<li>CORS is open: <code>Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *</code> on every response, preflights answer <code>204</code>.</li>
<li>Caching: <code>Cache-Control: public, max-age={{CACHE_TTL}}</code> on documents and <code>max-age={{SHA_CACHE_TTL}}</code> on checksum files; every response carries an <code>ETag</code>.</li>
<li>Compression: gzip (and brotli where available) on request.</li>
<li>Health: <code>GET /healthz</code> answers <code>{"status":"ok"}</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Access</h2>
{{ACCESS_HTML}}

<h2>Errors</h2>
<p>Every error is an <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457">RFC 9457 problem document</a> with the media type <code>application/problem+json</code>.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Status</th><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
<tr><td>400</td><td>bad_request</td><td>A query string or malformed request was sent.</td></tr>
<tr><td>401</td><td>unauthorized</td><td>A bearer token is required and was missing or invalid.</td></tr>
<tr><td>404</td><td>not_found</td><td>No such document in this endpoint.</td></tr>
<tr><td>405</td><td>method_not_allowed</td><td>Only GET, HEAD and OPTIONS are accepted.</td></tr>
<tr><td>429</td><td>rate_limited</td><td>The public budget for your address is used up; a <code>Retry-After</code> header is included.</td></tr>
<tr><td>503</td><td>unavailable</td><td>Temporary outage; retry after a moment.</td></tr>
</table>
{{#UNLESS IS_ROOT}}
<p><a href="/">All endpoints of {{DOMAIN}}</a></p>
{{/UNLESS}}
<footer>{{#IF ICON_URL}}<img src="{{ICON_URL}}" alt="">{{/IF}}Served by getBible · <a href="https://getBible.net">getBible.net</a> · <a href="https://getBible.net/mcp">MCP usage guide</a> · Requests carry an <code>X-Request-ID</code> header; quote it when reporting a problem.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
